theory|In E major, what is the ii chord?|F-sharp minor|A major|G-sharp major|B minor|F-sharp minor is the diatonic supertonic chord in E major.|MT
theory|Which note turns a C major triad into a C major-seventh chord?|B natural|B-flat|D natural|F-sharp|Adding B natural to C-E-G produces Cmaj7.|MT
theory|Which pitch is the ninth of a C9 chord?|D|E|B-flat|A|The ninth of a C dominant ninth chord is D.|MT
theory|Which dominant-seventh chord serves as V7 in A minor?|E7|D7|G7|A7|E7 resolves to A minor as its dominant seventh.|MT
theory|In D major, which major chord functions as V?|A major|G major|B major|E major|A major is built on D major's fifth scale degree.|MT
theory|What is the raised seventh scale degree of E harmonic minor?|D-sharp|D natural|C-sharp|F natural|E harmonic minor raises D to D-sharp.|MT
theory|Which pitch is the sixth degree of A Dorian?|F-sharp|F natural|G-sharp|E-flat|A Dorian has the notes A B C D E F-sharp G.|MT
theory|Which note is the flattened seventh in G Mixolydian?|F natural|F-sharp|E-flat|G-flat|G Mixolydian uses F natural rather than F-sharp.|MT
theory|Which pitch gives F Lydian its characteristic raised fourth?|B natural|B-flat|C-sharp|E-flat|F Lydian raises the fourth degree to B natural.|MT
theory|Which chord is spelled D, F-sharp, A, C?|D dominant seventh|D major seventh|D minor seventh|D diminished seventh|D-F-sharp-A-C forms a dominant seventh chord.|MT
theory|Which chord is spelled A, C, E, G?|A minor seventh|A major seventh|A dominant seventh|A half-diminished seventh|A-C-E-G forms an A minor seventh chord.|MT
theory|Which notes spell a B diminished triad?|B, D, F|B, D-sharp, F-sharp|B, D, G|B, E, F-sharp|B-D-F contains a minor third and diminished fifth.|MT
theory|Which note is in the bass of a second-inversion C major triad?|G|C|E|B|Second inversion places the fifth, G, below C and E.|MT
theory|Which note is in the bass of a first-inversion E minor triad?|G|E|B|D|First inversion places the chord's third, G, in the bass.|MT
theory|Which pitch is a tritone above D in equal temperament?|A-flat|G|A|B-flat|A tritone spans six semitones; D up six semitones is A-flat.|MT
theory|What is the interval from E up to C in the next octave?|Minor sixth|Major sixth|Perfect fifth|Minor seventh|E to the C above spans eight semitones, a minor sixth.|MT
theory|How many dotted-quarter beats are typically felt in 6/8 time?|Two|Three|Four|Six|Compound duple 6/8 groups its six eighth notes into two beats.|MT
theory|In 9/8 time, how many eighth notes fill one complete measure?|Nine|Six|Eight|Twelve|The numerator 9 indicates nine eighth-note units per bar.|MT
theory|How many quarter-note beats are in a bar of 5/4?|Five|Four|Six|Eight|A 5/4 measure holds five quarter-note units.|MT
theory|In ordinary simple meter, three eighth-note triplets occupy the time of how many quarter notes?|One|Two|Three|One half|Three eighth-note triplets fit in the duration of one quarter-note beat.|MT
